{"slug": "pla-goong-spicy-thai-shrimp-salad", "nyt_id": 1018217, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/1018217-pla-goong-spicy-thai-shrimp-salad", "name": "Pla Goong (Spicy Thai Shrimp Salad)", "author": "Francis Lam", "description": "This dish is somewhere between a shrimp salad and a ceviche – just-cooked shrimp dressed with a sour-savory-sweet mixture of lime, fish sauce, and sweet chile paste, then showered with herbs and chiles. In classic Thai fashion, it’s combination of many tastes, each moment on your palate different from the next. It’s a favorite of Pornpong Kanittanon, the Consul General of Thailand in New York, and the recipe is adapted from his wife, Jaisamarn. Francis Lam", "servings": {"text": "2 to 4 servings", "min": 2, "max": 4, "yield_type": "servings"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": null, "cook_minutes": null, "total_minutes": 35, "raw": {"total": "PT35M"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "Salt (optional)", "group": null, "quantity": null, "unit": null, "item": "salt", "preparation": null, "optional": true}, {"position": 2, "raw": "3 ounces lime juice (from about 3 limes)", "group": null, "quantity": 3.0, "unit": "oz", "item": "lime juice", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "3 tablespoons fish sauce", "group": null, "quantity": 3.0, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "fish sauce", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "1 ½ tablespoons sugar", "group": null, "quantity": 1.5, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "sugar", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "2 tablespoons nam prik pao (Thai chile paste in oil)", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "nam prik pao", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 6, "raw": "2 finely chopped Thai bird chiles, or to taste", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "unit": null, "item": "finely chopped thai bird chiles", "preparation": "or to taste", "optional": false}, {"position": 7, "raw": "1 pound large shrimp (1 ½ pounds if heads-on)", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": "lb", "item": "large shrimp", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 8, "raw": "⅔ cup very thinly sliced lemongrass (see note)", "group": null, "quantity": 0.6666666666666666, "unit": "cup", "item": "very thinly sliced lemongrass", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 9, "raw": "1 large shallot, thinly sliced", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": null, "item": "large shallot", "preparation": "thinly sliced", "optional": false}, {"position": 10, "raw": "½ cup roughly chopped cilantro", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "unit": "cup", "item": "roughly chopped cilantro", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 11, "raw": "½ cup whole mint leaves", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "unit": "cup", "item": "whole mint leaves", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 12, "raw": "6 makrut lime leaves, finely shredded", "group": null, "quantity": 6.0, "unit": null, "item": "makrut lime leaves", "preparation": "finely shredded", "optional": false}, {"position": 13, "raw": "Jasmine rice, for serving", "group": null, "quantity": null, "unit": null, "item": "jasmine rice", "preparation": "for serving", "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "Bring a pot of 3 quarts of water to a boil. (I like to salt the water like pasta water; Kanittanon does not add salt.)"}, {"position": 2, "text": "In a large bowl, combine the lime juice, fish sauce, sugar, nam prik pao and chopped chiles. Taste, and adjust with any of the ingredients, including salt. The sauce’s flavor should be led by sourness and savoriness, but with a good balance of sweetness and heat."}, {"position": 3, "text": "Cook the shrimp in the water until it just turns opaque, medium or medium-rare, about 1 minute. For better flavor, cook the shrimp with heads or shells on; peel when just cooled enough to handle."}, {"position": 4, "text": "Add the shrimp to the sauce while still warm and toss; the lime will continue to “cook” the shrimp like a ceviche. Add the lemongrass, shallot, cilantro, mint leaves and makrut lime leaves, reserving a little of each herb for garnish. Toss, and place on a dish; scatter the reserved herbs on top. Serve immediately with hot rice."}], "nutrition": {"source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving", "calories": 167.25, "protein_g": 25.2, "carbohydrates_g": 16.8, "fat_g": 0.9, "saturated_fat_g": 0.2, "unsaturated_fat_g": 0.3, "trans_fat_g": null, "cholesterol_mg": 182.6, "sodium_mg": 1205.0, "fiber_g": 2.1, "sugar_g": 8.3, "computed_with": null}, "tags": {"cuisine": ["thai"], "diet": [], "course": ["main-course"], "meal": [], "occasion": [], "other": ["fish-sauce", "jasmine-rice", "lemongrass", "shrimp"]}, "images": [{"url": "https://static01.nyt.com/images/2016/07/17/magazine/17eat/17eat-videoSixteenByNineJumbo1600-v4.jpg", "alt": "Pla Goong (Spicy Thai Shrimp Salad)", "primary": true}, {"url": "https://static01.nyt.com/images/2016/07/17/magazine/17eat/17eat-superJumbo-v3.jpg", "alt": "Pla Goong (Spicy Thai Shrimp Salad)", "primary": false}, {"url": "https://static01.nyt.com/images/2016/07/17/magazine/17eat/17eat-facebookJumbo-v3.jpg", "alt": "Pla Goong (Spicy Thai Shrimp Salad)", "primary": false}], "rating": {"average": 4.0, "count": 471}, "video_url": null, "comment_count": null, "published_at": "2016-07-17", "scraped_at": "2026-09-07T00:18:37Z", "scraper_version": "1.0.0"}
{"slug": "planters-punch", "nyt_id": 1016362, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/1016362-planters-punch", "name": "Planter’s Punch", "author": "Rosie Schaap", "description": "Good for serving one or serving a crowd, rummy planter’s punch is just off-sweet and surprisingly subtle.", "servings": {"text": "1 drink", "min": 1, "max": 1, "yield_type": "other"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": null, "cook_minutes": null, "total_minutes": 2, "raw": {"total": "PT2M"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "2 ounces dark rum", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "unit": "oz", "item": "dark rum", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "½ ounce fresh lime juice", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "unit": "oz", "item": "fresh lime juice", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "½ teaspoon simple syrup", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "unit": "tsp", "item": "simple syrup", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "1 dash Angostura bitters", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": "dash", "item": "angostura bitters", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "Soda water, to top (optional)", "group": null, "quantity": null, "unit": null, "item": "soda water", "preparation": "to top (optional)", "optional": true}, {"position": 6, "raw": "Pineapple slice, for garnish", "group": null, "quantity": null, "unit": null, "item": "pineapple slice", "preparation": "for garnish", "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "None"}], "nutrition": {"source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving", "calories": 227.0, "protein_g": 1.0, "carbohydrates_g": 25.3, "fat_g": 0.2, "saturated_fat_g": null, "unsaturated_fat_g": 0.1, "trans_fat_g": null, "cholesterol_mg": null, "sodium_mg": 79.0, "fiber_g": 2.4, "sugar_g": 19.0, "computed_with": null}, "tags": {"cuisine": [], "diet": [], "course": ["cocktails"], "meal": [], "occasion": [], "other": ["thanksgiving"]}, "images": [{"url": "https://static01.nyt.com/images/2014/05/20/multimedia/sumdrinks-planterpun-sit/sumdrinks-planterpun-sit-superJumbo.jpg", "alt": "", "primary": true}, {"url": "https://static01.nyt.com/images/2014/05/20/multimedia/sumdrinks-planterpun-sit/sumdrinks-planterpun-sit-facebookJumbo-v2.jpg", "alt": "", "primary": false}], "rating": {"average": 4.0, "count": 115}, "video_url": "https://vp.nyt.com/video/2014/05/20/28283_1_sumdrinks-planterpun-sit_wg_480p.mp4", "comment_count": null, "published_at": "2014-05-17", "scraped_at": "2026-09-07T03:09:50Z", "scraper_version": "1.0.0"}
{"slug": "plum-and-fig-crumble-with-quinoa-oat-topping", "nyt_id": 1013290, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/1013290-plum-and-fig-crumble-with-quinoa-oat-topping", "name": "Plum and Fig Crumble With Quinoa-Oat Topping", "author": "Martha Rose Shulman", "description": "At a farmers’ market, seek out sweet plums, ripe but firm, for this dazzling crumble. I also like a reddish, pink-fleshed hybrid called a plumcot, which is an apricot-plum hybrid. Plums are high in antioxidants called phenols, a very good source of vitamin C and, to a lesser extent, of vitamin A, riboflavin and potassium.", "servings": {"text": "8 servings", "min": 8, "max": 8, "yield_type": "servings"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": null, "cook_minutes": null, "total_minutes": 45, "raw": {"total": "PT45M"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "2 pounds plums, preferably a red-fleshed variety like elephant hearts, or plumcots, pitted and cut into sixths", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "unit": "lb", "item": "plums", "preparation": "preferably a red-fleshed variety like elephant hearts, or plumcots, pitted and cut into sixths", "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "6 fresh figs, stemmed and cut in half", "group": null, "quantity": 6.0, "unit": null, "item": "fresh figs", "preparation": "stemmed and cut in half", "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "2 tablespoons sugar, preferably organic", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "sugar", "preparation": "preferably organic", "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "2 teaspoons rose water", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "unit": "tsp", "item": "rose water", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "½ teaspoon cinnamon", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "unit": "tsp", "item": "cinnamon", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 6, "raw": "1 tablespoon plum brandy or red wine (optional)", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "plum brandy or red wine", "preparation": null, "optional": true}, {"position": 7, "raw": "1 teaspoon arrowroot", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": "tsp", "item": "arrowroot", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 8, "raw": "1 batch quinoa-oat crumble topping", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": null, "item": "batch quinoa-oat crumble topping", "preparation": null, "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "In a large bowl, mix together the plums, figs, rose water, cinnamon and brandy or wine. Cover and let sit for one to two hours, in or out of the refrigerator."}, {"position": 2, "text": "Preheat the oven to 350 degrees. Butter a two-quart baking dish. Whisk the arrowroot into the juice, and scrape the fruit and all of the juice into the baking dish. Set the baking dish on a baking sheet for easier handling, and place in the oven. Bake 20 to 25 minutes until the fruit is bubbling and the liquid syrupy. Remove from the oven, and allow to cool if desired."}, {"position": 3, "text": "About 30 minutes before serving, spread the crumble topping over the plum mixture in an even layer. Bake 20 minutes, or until the fruit is bubbling and the topping is nicely browned. Remove from the heat, and allow to cool for at least 10 minutes before serving."}], "nutrition": {"source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving", "calories": 97.375, "protein_g": 1.1, "carbohydrates_g": 23.6, "fat_g": 0.4, "saturated_fat_g": null, "unsaturated_fat_g": 0.1, "trans_fat_g": null, "cholesterol_mg": null, "sodium_mg": 0.6, "fiber_g": 2.8, "sugar_g": 20.7, "computed_with": null}, "tags": {"cuisine": [], "diet": [], "course": ["crumble-dessert"], "meal": [], "occasion": [], "other": ["fig", "plum", "summer"]}, "images": [{"url": "https://static01.nyt.com/images/2010/10/05/science/06recipehealth600/06recipehealth600-superJumbo.jpg", "alt": "", "primary": true}, {"url": "https://static01.nyt.com/images/2010/10/05/science/06recipehealth600/06recipehealth600-facebookJumbo-v2.jpg", "alt": "", "primary": false}], "rating": {"average": 3.0, "count": 29}, "video_url": null, "comment_count": null, "published_at": "2010-10-06", "scraped_at": "2026-09-07T01:47:39Z", "scraper_version": "1.0.0"}
{"slug": "plum-and-red-wine-soup", "nyt_id": 1012734, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/1012734-plum-and-red-wine-soup", "name": "Plum and Red Wine Soup", "author": "Martha Rose Shulman", "description": "You could also call this ruby-colored, jam-like soup a compote. Look for plums with deep red flesh.", "servings": {"text": "6 servings", "min": 6, "max": 6, "yield_type": "servings"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": null, "cook_minutes": null, "total_minutes": 100, "raw": {"total": "PT1H40M"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "3 pounds ripe purple-skinned, red-fleshed plums", "group": null, "quantity": 3.0, "unit": "lb", "item": "ripe purple-skinned", "preparation": "red-fleshed plums", "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "¼ cup mild honey", "group": null, "quantity": 0.25, "unit": "cup", "item": "mild honey", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "½ teaspoon vanilla extract", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "unit": "tsp", "item": "vanilla extract", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "1 inch cinnamon stick", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": null, "item": "inch cinnamon stick", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "⅛ teaspoon freshly grated nutmeg", "group": null, "quantity": 0.125, "unit": "tsp", "item": "freshly grated nutmeg", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 6, "raw": "2 strips orange zest", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "unit": null, "item": "strips orange zest", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 7, "raw": "1 sprig rose geranium (optional)", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": "sprig", "item": "rose geranium", "preparation": null, "optional": true}, {"position": 8, "raw": "¾ cup fruity red wine, such as a Beaujolais", "group": null, "quantity": 0.75, "unit": "cup", "item": "fruity red wine", "preparation": "such as a Beaujolais", "optional": false}, {"position": 9, "raw": "¾ cup freshly squeezed orange juice", "group": null, "quantity": 0.75, "unit": "cup", "item": "freshly squeezed orange juice", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 10, "raw": "2 lighter-fleshed plums, very thinly sliced", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "unit": null, "item": "lighter-fleshed plums", "preparation": "very thinly sliced", "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "Cut the plums in half, cutting around the sides of the pits. You will remove the pits after the plums have simmered."}, {"position": 2, "text": "Combine the plums with the honey, vanilla extract, cinnamon stick, nutmeg, orange zest, rose geranium, wine and ½ cup of the orange juice in a heavy, medium saucepan. Bring to a boil, reduce the heat, cover and simmer for 30 minutes. Remove from the heat. Remove the cinnamon stick, rose geranium sprig and orange zest."}, {"position": 3, "text": "Allow to cool, then remove the pits from the plums and transfer to a food mill fitted with the medium blade. Press the plums through the food mill into a bowl. Whisk the mixture to amalgamate. Cover and chill for at least an hour and for up to a day."}, {"position": 4, "text": "Just before serving, whisk in the remaining orange juice. Ladle into bowls. Garnish with thin slices of lighter-fleshed plums and serve."}], "nutrition": {"source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving", "calories": 301.6666666666667, "protein_g": 2.1, "carbohydrates_g": 47.8, "fat_g": 0.8, "saturated_fat_g": 0.1, "unsaturated_fat_g": 0.1, "trans_fat_g": null, "cholesterol_mg": null, "sodium_mg": 8.4, "fiber_g": 3.9, "sugar_g": 40.3, "computed_with": null}, "tags": {"cuisine": [], "diet": [], "course": ["dessert-soup"], "meal": [], "occasion": [], "other": ["easy", "great-leftovers", "plum", "red-wine", "summer"]}, "images": [{"url": "https://static01.nyt.com/images/2009/08/19/health/19recipehealth_600/19recipehealth_600-superJumbo.jpg", "alt": "", "primary": true}, {"url": "https://static01.nyt.com/images/2009/08/19/health/19recipehealth_600/19recipehealth_600-facebookJumbo-v2.jpg", "alt": "", "primary": false}], "rating": {"average": 4.0, "count": 13}, "video_url": null, "comment_count": null, "published_at": "2009-08-19", "scraped_at": "2026-09-07T01:28:56Z", "scraper_version": "1.0.0"}
{"slug": "plum-chutney-crumb-pie", "nyt_id": 1014846, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/1014846-plum-chutney-crumb-pie", "name": "Plum Chutney Crumb Pie", "author": "Melissa Clark", "description": "If you’ve never made chutney, you might think it to be one of those long-simmering, involved recipes that take the better part of a day. Really, making chutney is no harder than making applesauce. All you do is cook down the fruit with spices, herbs, sugar and, very important, a little vinegar to accentuate the tang, and you’re done. The intriguing flavor comes from the combination of ingredients, not from a complicated technique.", "servings": {"text": "1 9-inch pie", "min": 1, "max": 1, "yield_type": "other"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": null, "cook_minutes": null, "total_minutes": 120, "raw": {"total": "PT2H"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "170 grams all-purpose flour (about 1 ¼ cups), more as needed for rolling out dough", "group": null, "quantity": 170.0, "unit": "g", "item": "all-purpose flour", "preparation": "more as needed for rolling out dough", "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "1 gram fine sea salt (about ¼ teaspoon)", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": "g", "item": "fine sea salt", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "10 tablespoons unsalted butter, preferably a high-fat, European-style butter, chilled and cut into ½-inch pieces", "group": null, "quantity": 10.0, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "unsalted butter", "preparation": "preferably a high-fat, European-style butter, chilled and cut into ½-inch pieces", "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "2 tablespoons cider vinegar", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "cider vinegar", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "70 grams light brown sugar (about ⅓ cup)", "group": null, "quantity": 70.0, "unit": "g", "item": "light brown sugar", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 6, "raw": "1 star anise pod", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": null, "item": "star anise pod", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 7, "raw": "1 cinnamon stick (2 inches long)", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": null, "item": "cinnamon stick", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 8, "raw": "1 small sprig fresh rosemary", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": null, "item": "small sprig fresh rosemary", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 9, "raw": "1 teaspoon grated fresh ginger root", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": "tsp", "item": "grated fresh ginger root", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 10, "raw": "1 gram black pepper (about ½ teaspoon)", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": "g", "item": "black pepper", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 11, "raw": "2 grams ground cardamom (about ½ teaspoon)", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "unit": "g", "item": "ground cardamom", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 12, "raw": "1 gram fine sea salt (about ¼ teaspoon)", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": "g", "item": "fine sea salt", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 13, "raw": "3 pounds ripe plums, pitted and sliced (about 6 cups)", "group": null, "quantity": 3.0, "unit": "lb", "item": "ripe plums", "preparation": "pitted and sliced (about 6 cups)", "optional": false}, {"position": 14, "raw": "100 grams granulated sugar (about ½ cup), more to taste", "group": null, "quantity": 100.0, "unit": "g", "item": "granulated sugar", "preparation": "more to taste", "optional": false}, {"position": 15, "raw": "1 teaspoon freshly grated orange zest", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": "tsp", "item": "freshly grated orange zest", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 16, "raw": "25 grams instant tapioca (about 2 tablespoons)", "group": null, "quantity": 25.0, "unit": "g", "item": "instant tapioca", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 17, "raw": "90 grams all-purpose flour (about ¾ cup)", "group": null, "quantity": 90.0, "unit": "g", "item": "all-purpose flour", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 18, "raw": "100 grams dark brown sugar (about ½ cup)", "group": null, "quantity": 100.0, "unit": "g", "item": "dark brown sugar", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 19, "raw": "5 grams cinnamon (about 1 teaspoon)", "group": null, "quantity": 5.0, "unit": "g", "item": "cinnamon", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 20, "raw": "Pinch ground cloves", "group": null, "quantity": null, "unit": null, "item": "pinch ground cloves", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 21, "raw": "1 gram fine sea salt (about ¼ teaspoon)", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": "g", "item": "fine sea salt", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 22, "raw": "5 tablespoons unsalted butter, cut into pieces", "group": null, "quantity": 5.0, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "unsalted butter", "preparation": "cut into pieces", "optional": false}, {"position": 23, "raw": "Vanilla ice cream, for serving (optional)", "group": null, "quantity": null, "unit": null, "item": "vanilla ice cream", "preparation": "for serving (optional)", "optional": true}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "Make the crust: In a food processor, briefly pulse together flour and salt. Add butter and pulse until mixture forms chickpea-size pieces (3 to 5 one-second pulses). Add ice water 1 tablespoon at a time, up to 6 tablespoons, pulsing occasionally until mixture is just moist enough to hold together. Form dough into a ball, wrap with plastic and flatten into a disk. Refrigerate at least 1 hour."}, {"position": 2, "text": "Make the chutney: In a medium saucepan over medium heat, bring vinegar, 2 tablespoons water, brown sugar, star anise, cinnamon stick, rosemary sprig, ginger root, pepper, cardamom and salt to a simmer, stirring to help dissolve sugar. Add a third of the plums and let mixture simmer until thickened, stirring frequently, 20 to 30 minutes. Let cool, then discard star anise, cinnamon stick and rosemary."}, {"position": 3, "text": "Meanwhile, toss remaining plums, granulated sugar, orange zest and tapioca in a bowl and let sit for 20 minutes. (If your plums are tart, add more sugar to taste.)"}, {"position": 4, "text": "Lightly flour a work surface and rolling pin. Gently roll out dough to fit a 9-inch pie pan, dusting with flour if dough is sticking. Fold dough in half and transfer to pie pan. Carefully press crust into pan and crimp edges. Return pie to refrigerator for 20 minutes. While crust chills, heat oven to 400 degrees."}, {"position": 5, "text": "Gently press foil into pie crust and fill with pie weights or dried beans. Transfer to oven and bake for 18 minutes. Remove the foil and pie weights and bake for another 5 to 10 minutes, or until crust is a light golden brown. Transfer to a rack to cool slightly."}, {"position": 6, "text": "Meanwhile, prepare the crumb topping: In a small bowl, combine flour, brown sugar, cinnamon, cloves and salt. Using your hands, work in butter until the dry ingredients are completely incorporated into butter and large, marble-size clumps form when pinched. Let sit in refrigerator while assembling pie."}, {"position": 7, "text": "Mix chutney into uncooked plums. Pour filling into crust and cover with crumb topping. Turn oven down to 350 degrees and place pie on a baking sheet on middle rack in oven. Bake pie for 1 to 1 ½ hours or until fruit is bubbling and top is golden brown. Serve warm or at room temperature, with vanilla ice cream if you like."}], "nutrition": null, "tags": {"cuisine": [], "diet": [], "course": ["dessert-pie"], "meal": [], "occasion": [], "other": ["food-processor", "plum", "summer"]}, "images": [{"url": "https://static01.nyt.com/images/2013/07/03/dining/03APPE_SPAN/03APPE_SPAN-superJumbo.jpg", "alt": "Plum chutney crumb pie.", "primary": true}, {"url": "https://static01.nyt.com/images/2013/07/03/dining/03APPE_SPAN/03APPE_SPAN-facebookJumbo-v2.jpg", "alt": "Plum chutney crumb pie.", "primary": false}], "rating": {"average": 4.0, "count": 135}, "video_url": null, "comment_count": null, "published_at": "2013-07-03", "scraped_at": "2026-09-07T02:28:36Z", "scraper_version": "1.0.0"}
